| $V(s)$ | **State-Value** | Expected return from state $s$ following policy $\pi$ (average of all possible paths). | $V^\pi(s) = \mathbb{E}_\pi [G_t \| S_t = s]$ |
| $Q(s, a)$ | **Action-Value** | Expected return from state $s$, taking action $a$. | $Q^\pi(s, a) = \mathbb{E}_\pi [G_t \| S_t = s, A_t = a]$ |
| $\gamma$ | **Discount Factor** | Weight given to future rewards ($0 \le \gamma \le 1$). | Determines the agent's horizon/foresight. |
| $\alpha$ | **Learning Rate** | Step size for updating value estimates. | Controls the speed of information override. |
| $\epsilon$ | **Epsilon** | Probability of picking a random action. | Manages the Exploration vs. Exploitation trade-off. |
| $\delta_t$ | **TD Error** | Difference between the estimate and the target. | $\delta_t = R_{t+1} + \gamma V(S_{t+1}) - V(S_t)$ |
| $P(s'\|s, a)$ | **Dynamics** | Transition probability to next state $s'$. | Defines environmental "physics." |
